{
    "background_story": "In ancient Celtic lore, Kora was a mystical being said to possess the essence of the mezereon, a rare and sacred plant with powers of protection and healing. According to legend, Kora was born from the mezereon's roots, and her spirit was woven into the fabric of the forest. With skin as pale as the mezereon's blooms and hair as dark as the forest's shadows, Kora roamed the woods, using her gifts to defend the land against harm. She was said to be able to communicate with the ancient trees and summon the mezereon's potency to mend the wounds of the forest creatures. Kora's connection to the mezereon made her a revered guardian, and her name became synonymous with the mystical powers of the natural world.",
